#X text 215 83 || Versions <5.0;
#X text 215 108 The BCM283x SoC supports 2 hardware PWM channels. By
default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 215 148 • PWM0 = GPIO12/GPIO18;
#X text 215 173 • PWM1 = GPIO13/GPIO19;
#X text 215 198 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 215 238 Note: the Raspberry Pi?s analog audio output uses both
PWM channels. Playing audio and simultaneously accessing a PWM channel
may cause issues.;
#X text 215 293 ~;
#X text 215 318 || Raspberry Pi 5 and later;
#X text 215 343 The Raspberry Pi 5 support 4 hardware PWM channels.
By default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 215 383 • PWM0 = GPIO12;
#X text 215 408 • PWM1 = GPIO13;
#X text 215 433 • PWM2 = GPIO18;
#X text 215 458 • PWM3 = GPIO19;
#X text 215 483 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 215 523 ~;
#X text 215 548 Some of the GPIO pins capable of supporting hardware
PWM can also be configured for use with other peripherals. Be careful
not to enable two peripherals on the same pin at the same time.;
